cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "RecurringAlignment: Lexical Drift Detection and In-Context Realignment for AI-Assistant Conversations"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Frohman
    given-names: Benjamin
    email: frohmanbenjamin@gmail.com
version: 0.2.1
date-released: 2026-11-01
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/BenFrohman/RecurringAlignment"
abstract: >-
  A TypeScript toolkit that scores each assistant turn of a conversation for drift from a
  user-defined anchor (goals, constraints, persona, decisions) using TF-IDF/cosine similarity
  and rule heuristics, generates compact realignment prompts for in-context correction, and
  rebuilds a clean resume state after drift (Drift Replay).
keywords:
  - large language models
  - conversational AI
  - drift detection
  - context management
  - prompt engineering
  - TF-IDF
